course: biology
lesson: 129
title: The penguins of Madagascar: real penguins and chimps
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: In Madagascar, four penguins plot clever escapes, flap their flippers and fail to fly, and dream of reaching Antarctica, while the chimps Mason and Phil read the newspaper.
explain: Real penguins cannot fly in the air, but they «fly» under water, flapping stiff flippers that once were wings, and gentoo penguins are the fastest swimming birds of all.
explain: Wild penguins live only in the southern half of the world, mostly around Antarctica but also on warm beaches in South Africa, and one kind lives right on the equator, kept cool by cold sea currents.
explain: Their black and white suits are camouflage: from below a white belly matches the bright sky, and from above a black back matches the dark sea.
explain: Real chimps cannot read newspapers, but they are clever apes that learn symbols, fish for termites with sticks and crack nuts with stones.
fact: Wild penguins live only in the southern half of the world; none live in Madagascar or at the North Pole.
fact: The Galapagos penguin lives on the equator, kept cool by cold ocean currents.
fact: Penguins «fly» under water with stiff, short flippers, and gentoo penguins can swim at about 35 km per hour, faster than any other bird under water.
fact: Penguins waddle because their legs are short and set far back, and waddling actually saves energy; their knees are hidden under their feathers.
fact: Penguins toboggan on their bellies, pushing with feet and flippers, because sliding is quicker and uses less energy than walking on snow.
fact: A penguin's black back and white belly are camouflage called countershading, which many fish and sharks have too.
fact: Penguins can drink sea water, because a special gland above the eyes removes extra salt, which drips out from the beak.
fact: Each chick has its own voice, and its parents recognise it among thousands of others in a noisy colony.
fact: Emperor penguin fathers keep the egg warm on their feet for about two months without eating.
fact: Real penguins do not plan schemes, but they are social and curious and learn routes and routines; Adelie penguins steal nest stones from each other.
fact: Real chimps cannot read, but they can learn many symbols to ask for things, and wild chimps use sticks to fish for termites and stones to crack nuts.
fact: Emperor penguins huddle in big groups and shuffle so that everyone takes turns in the warm middle, which can be warmer than a summer day.
fact: Not all penguins need ice: African penguins live on warm coasts of South Africa and Namibia and bray like donkeys.
exercise: Where do wild penguins live? | Only in the southern half of the world | At the North Pole, next to the polar bears | All over Madagascar | In every ocean north and south
exercise: Which penguin lives right on the equator? | The Galapagos penguin | The big emperor penguin | The little African penguin | No penguin lives there
exercise: Can penguins fly? | Not in the air, but they «fly» under water with their flippers | Yes, short distances like chickens, flapping from rock to rock | Yes, high over the sea | No, and they cannot swim either
exercise: About how fast can a gentoo penguin swim? | About 35 km per hour | Only about 3 km per hour | About 135 km per hour | Only about 1 km per hour
exercise: Why do penguins waddle? | Their legs are short and set far back, and waddling saves energy | They have no knees at all, so their legs cannot bend | Their feet are frozen stiff from standing on the ice for so long | They are always tired
exercise: Why does a penguin slide on its belly down a snowy slope? | It is quicker and uses less energy than walking | To clean its belly feathers | To keep its belly cool | To dig a nest in the snow
exercise: Why are penguins black and white? | Camouflage: dark backs match the sea from above and white bellies the sky from below | To look smart like waiters, which helps them find a mate | So they can see each other clearly in the dark during the long polar winter nights | Because they eat black and white fish
exercise: What is dark-on-top, light-below camouflage called? | Countershading | Mimicry | Hibernation | Moulting
exercise: How can a penguin drink salty sea water? | A gland above its eyes removes the extra salt | It spits out all the salt again with its tongue and beak | Salt does not harm any animal | It only drinks melted snow
exercise: How do penguin parents find their own chick in a huge colony? | Each chick has its own voice | Each chick wears a different colour | They count all the chicks one by one | They wait until the others leave
exercise: How long does an emperor father keep the egg warm on his feet? | About two months, without eating | About two weeks, while the mother sits beside him | About two days | About two years
exercise: Do real penguins plan clever escapes like in the film? | No, but they are curious and learn routes and routines | Yes, they draw maps in the snow with their beaks before escaping | Yes, they build boats | Yes, they read instructions
exercise: What do Adelie penguins steal from each other? | Nest stones | Fish | Eggs | Feathers
exercise: Can real chimps read newspapers? | No, but they can learn many symbols to ask for things | Yes, every morning | Yes, but only the big headlines and the comics on the back page | No, and they cannot learn anything
exercise: What tools do wild chimps use? | Sticks to fish for termites and stones to crack nuts | Hammers and nails that they take from people's camps at night | Spoons and forks | No tools at all
exercise: Why do emperor penguins shuffle around in their huddle? | So everyone takes turns in the warm middle | To find their chicks in the crowd | To dance for the colony | To scare off seals that wait in the water nearby
exercise: Do all penguins need ice and cold water? | No, African penguins live on warm coasts | Yes, every penguin needs ice, or it gets ill | Yes, or they melt | No, penguins live in deserts
test: «polar bears eat penguins at the North Pole, saw it on a mug» What is right? | Impossible: wild penguins live only in the south and polar bears in the north | True, it happens every day on the ice, because both of them live at the North Pole | True, but only in summer | True, polar bears love penguins
test: «4 penguins from the film, how many flippers» How many? | 8 | 4 | 16 | 12
test: «6 penguins and 2 zookeepers, how many legs» How many? | 16 | 32 | 12 | 20
test: «penguins are so slow lol, they can't even walk properly» What is right? | Waddling saves energy, and under water they are fast swimmers | Right, they are slow everywhere, on land and under the sea as well | Right, they cannot swim either | Right, they have no legs
test: What would happen to a penguin's camouflage if it were white on top and black below? | Seals below and birds above would spot it more easily | It would be even harder to see from both above and below | Nothing would change | It would turn invisible
test: «penguin's drinking seawater, it'll get sick, stop it» What is right? | It is fine; a gland above its eyes takes out the extra salt | Yes, stop it at once | Yes, penguins need clean tap water, salt water makes them ill | Yes, salt makes them float away
test: «the middle of a penguin huddle is freezing, right» What is right? | The middle can be warmer than a summer day | Yes, the middle is colder than the outside, as no sun reaches it | Yes, it turns to ice | Penguins never huddle
test: «penguin at the zoo's on a warm beach, it'll melt» What is right? | African penguins live on warm coasts naturally | It must be moved to ice at once | Penguins melt in the sun | All zoo penguins are fake
test: «chimp in the film reads the paper, so chimps can read» What is right? | Real chimps cannot read but learn symbols and use tools | Right, chimps read slowly | Right, they read picture books | Wrong, chimps cannot learn anything at all, not even symbols
test: «penguins all look the same, how does mum find her kid» What is right? | She knows her chick's voice | She counts every chick in the colony | She smells its feathers only | She never finds it, so another penguin feeds it
test: An emperor father keeps his egg on his feet for two months. What can't he do in that time? | Go to sea to eat | Stand up straight | Make any sound at all | Sleep in the colony
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning the geographical distribution of wild penguins. | They are confined to the southern half of the world | They inhabit both polar regions in equal number | They are found in abundance upon Madagascar | They occur in every ocean of the northern half of the world
exam: Identify the principal reason for the black and white colouration of the penguin. | It constitutes camouflage, the dark back matching the sea and the pale belly the sky | It serves to distinguish the males, which are black, from the females, which are white | It permits penguins to perceive one another in darkness | It derives from the colouration of the fish upon which they feed
exam: Ascertain the means by which the penguin is enabled to consume sea water. | A gland situated above the eyes removes the excess of salt | The penguin expels the salt by means of its tongue | Salt is harmless to all animals in any quantity | The penguin consumes only melted snow
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the abilities of the chimpanzee? | It cannot read, but may learn numerous symbols and employs sticks and stones as tools | It reads printed matter with fluency, as shown in the film, and writes a few simple words | It employs no tools of any description | It is incapable of learning from others of its kind
